  "name": "PICES Scientific Report No. 18 (2001) - Proceedings of the PICES/CoML/IPRC Workshop on \"Impact of Climate Variability on Observation and Prediction of Ecosystem and Biodiversity Changes in the North Pacific\" / edited by Vera Alexander ... [et al.]",
  "description": "Define existing observation and prediction system (regional and basin-scales), identify needed improvements to the existing system for increasing the understanding of biodiversity and climate-linked changes in biodiversity, and nominate existing time series and predictions for inclusion into a PICES Ecosystem Status Report. International workshop on \"Impact of Climate Variability on Observation and Prediction of Ecosystem and Biodiversity Changes in the North Pacific\" co-sponsored by the Census of Marine Life (CoML) and the International Pacific Research Center (IPRC), held from March 7-9, 2001, at the East-West Center, Honolulu, Hawaii. LC Call No. GC781 .P535 no.18. ISBN 0968510086\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To review the goals and strategies for observing North Pacific marine ecosystem and their biodiversity and to improve our ability to predict ecosystem change.",
